            <ArticleTitle>Thunderclap headache and reversible segmental cerebral vasoconstriction associated with use of oxymetazoline nasal spray.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>593-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oxymetazoline is a sympathomimetic amine found in over-the-counter nasal decongestants. We report a case of chronic use of nasal oxymetazoline associated with thunderclap headache due to reversible segmental intracranial vasoconstriction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
